  "final_message": "`POST /orders` now accepts an optional `couponCode`. It is stored on the order and included in the `OrderPlaced` event. Typecheck, arch and the 39 existing tests pass, but I didn't add tests for the new field.\n\n- **Request parsing** (`src/api/requestParsing.ts`): reads `couponCode` as an optional string. A non-string value returns 400.\n- **Validation and storage** (`src/core/order.ts`): if present, the code must be non-blank and at most 64 characters, otherwise 400. That 64-character cap is my own choice (`LIMITS.maxCouponCodeLength`), so change it if you have a real rule. The field is stored only when supplied.\n- **Event** (`src/core/events.ts`): `OrderPlaced` includes `couponCode` only when the order has one. I left `schemaVersion` at 3 because the field is optional and additive. Bump it if your consumers need an explicit signal.\n\nI didn't touch the response body for `POST /orders`, since the documented shape doesn't list the coupon. I also didn't check `GET /orders/{id}` or the repository adapters, so I haven't confirmed that `GET` returns the stored coupon. Say if you want it added to the responses.",
